  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the most critical need is to establish a clean, well-defined baseline for the multimodal setting. config_007 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted) uses the most standard and well-understood component at every design dimension: a simple linear RNA encoder (pca_n2000), a widely-used image backbone (resnet50), a single profile (avoiding confounding from multiprofile aggregation), and a simple weighted fusion. This gives a reference performance against which all future experiments can isolate the effect of changing one dimension (e.g., swapping to scgpt, adding multiprofile with avgpool, or trying concat fusion). Starting with this 'control' configuration maximizes the information gained per experiment, because every subsequent result can be interpreted as a delta from a known anchor, reducing uncertainty about which design choices matter."
}

